@page "/components/date-picker"

<PageTitle>Date Picker — Unpoly.Blazor.Shadcn</PageTitle>

<h1 class="doc-h1">Date Picker</h1>
<p class="doc-lede">
    <code>&lt;input type="date"&gt;</code>, which already has a calendar, a keyboard, a locale and
    a mobile picker. Air Datepicker enhances it where a range or a disabled-day rule is needed; the
    input posts either way, and with scripting off it is still a date field rather than a text box.
</p>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Basic</h2>
<Example Source="DatePickerBasic.razor"><DatePickerBasic /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Range Picker</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    Two inputs with two names, which is what a server wants to read — and what lets the second one
    refuse a date before the first without any script.
</p>
<Example Source="DatePickerRange.razor"><DatePickerRange /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Date of Birth</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    The case where a calendar is the wrong control: nobody wants to page back three hundred months.
    <code>autocomplete="bday"</code> lets the browser fill it.
</p>
<Example Source="DatePickerBirthday.razor"><DatePickerBirthday /></Example>

